paragraph.math:
$$\begin{array}{lll}
      {\textbf{x} = \left\lbrack \begin{array}{l}
      x_{1} \\
      x_{2} \\
      x_{3}
      \end{array} \right\rbrack} & = & {\left\lbrack \begin{array}{l}
      {.3x_{2} + .2x_{2}} \\
      x_{2} \\
      x_{3}
      \end{array} \right\rbrack = \left\lbrack \begin{array}{r}
      {.3x_{2}} \\
      x_{2} \\
      0
      \end{array} \right\rbrack + \left\lbrack \begin{array}{r}
      {.2x3} \\
      0 \\
      x_{3}
      \end{array} \right\rbrack} \\
       & = & {x_{2}\left\lbrack \begin{array}{l}
      .3 \\
      1 \\
      0
      \end{array} \right\rbrack + x_{3}\left\lbrack \begin{array}{l}
      .2 \\
      0 \\
      1
      \end{array} \right\rbrack\,\,\text{(with~}x_{2}\text{,~}x_{\text{3}}\,\text{free)}} \\
       & & {\begin{array}{llll}
       & \overset{  \,\, \uparrow}{\textbf{ }\textbf{\, u}} & & 
      \end{array}\overset{     \,\, \uparrow}{\textbf{ }\textbf{\,\,\,  \,v}}}
      \end{array}$$

statement.paragraph:
Given $A = \,\,\begin{bmatrix}
      {- 2} & {- 6} \\
      7 & 21 \\
      {- 3} & {- 9}
      \end{bmatrix}\,,$ find one nontrivial solution of $A\mathbf{x} = 0$ by inspection. [Hint:Think of the equation $A\mathbf{x} = 0$ written as a vector equation.]

Given $A = \,\,\begin{bmatrix}
      4 & {- 6} \\
      {- 8} & 12 \\
      6 & {- 9}
      \end{bmatrix}\,,$, find one nontrivial solution of $A\mathbf{x} = 0$ by inspection.
